# docs/specs/081-hours-calculator.md: prettier's markdown printer is not
# idempotent on one paragraph in this file (unicode fractions ⅙½⅚ and a
# minus sign − appear to confuse its print-width line-wrap calculation) —
# a first --write preserves the nested list correctly, but a second
# --write (which `--check` effectively requires to be stable) silently
# flattens the list into inline text, destroying content. Exempted rather
# than accepting the destructive rewrite. See PR for #89.
docs/specs/081-hours-calculator.md

# pnpm-lock.yaml is generated by pnpm and must stay byte-identical to what pnpm
# writes. It is not in `format:check`'s globs, but lint-staged's `*.{md,json,yml,
# yaml}` hook matches it by extension — so a LOCAL commit touching the lockfile
# reformats it while a Renovate PR (no local hooks) does not. The two forms then
# fight: every future lockfile PR would carry a ~5000-line format revert on top
# of its real delta, and nothing in CI would ever see it. Found in the review of
# PR #241 (#240).
pnpm-lock.yaml

